.TH BADAPPLESTEIN-ENCODE 1 "July 2026" "BadAppleStein 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
badapplestein-encode \- encode a video using a source library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B badapplestein encode
.RB [ options ]
.I input_video
.I output_video
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B badapplestein encode
runs a two\-stage pipeline to reconstruct a video as a mosaic of source library
pages.
.TP
.B Stage 1 (arrange)
Every frame of
.I input_video
is divided into a grid of cells.
Each cell is matched against the feature descriptors in the source library to
find the closest\-matching page.
The result is written to an intermediate manifest.
.TP
.B Stage 2 (render)
The matched pages are sampled, scaled, and composited into a grid at the
target resolution.
The assembled frames are encoded into
.I output_video
using the selected codec.
.PP
Intermediate manifests are deleted automatically after a successful render unless
.B \-\-keep\-manifests
is specified.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-library " " \fIdir\fR
Path to the source library directory.
Default:
.BR ~/.badapplestein/library/ .
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " " \fIname\fR
Resolution preset.
Valid values:
.BR 8k (7680x4320),
.BR 4k (3840x2160),
.BR 1080p (1920x1080),
.BR 720p (1280x720).
Default: determined by the input video dimensions.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIpx\fR
Output width in pixels.
Overrides the preset.
.TP
.BR \-\-height " " \fIpx\fR
Output height in pixels.
Overrides the preset.
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " " \fIn\fR
Output frames per second.
Defaults to the input video frame rate.
.TP
.BR \-\-codec " " \fIname\fR
Video codec.
Options:
.BR prores ,
.BR h264 .
Auto\-detected when omitted (see
.B HARDWARE
below).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hw
Disable hardware acceleration.
Forces software ProRes encoding.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-frames " " \fIn\fR
Maximum number of frames to process.
Useful for quick previews and testing.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIn\fR
Number of worker threads for matching and rendering.
Defaults to the number of available CPU cores.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-manifests
Retain intermediate manifest files after rendering.
Useful for debugging or re\-rendering without re\-matching.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print detailed progress to stderr, including frame\-by\-frame match statistics.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress all non\-error output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON progress messages to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH HARDWARE
.B badapplestein encode
auto\-detects the best available hardware encoder at startup:
.TP
.B VideoToolbox (macOS)
Used for ProRes encoding when available.
Checked first on macOS.
.TP
.B VAAPI / NVENC (Linux)
Used for H.264 encoding on systems with Intel (VAAPI) or NVIDIA (NVENC) GPU
support.
.TP
.B Software fallback
When no hardware encoder is found, the tool falls back to software\-encoded
ProRes.
.PP
Use
.B \-\-no\-hw
to bypass hardware detection entirely, or
.B \-\-codec
to force a specific encoder.
.SH PERFORMANCE
.TP
.B Use a local library
Place the library on fast local storage (SSD) rather than a network mount.
Matching is I/O\-bound during the arrange stage.
.TP
.B Limit threads
On machines with many cores, setting
.B \-\-threads
to slightly below the core count can improve throughput by leaving headroom for
the OS.
.TP
.B Preview first
Use
.B \-\-max\-frames
and a lower preset (720p) to verify results before committing to a full\-length
encode.
.TP
.B Keep manifests
Run with
.B \-\-keep\-manifests
during development so the arrange stage can be skipped on subsequent renders.
.SH EXAMPLES
Encode at the default resolution:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode input.mov output.mov
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode at 4K using H.264:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-preset 4k \-\-codec h264 input.mov output.mp4
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick 720p preview, first 100 frames:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-preset 720p \-\-max\-frames 100 input.mov preview.mov
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode with software\-only ProRes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-no\-hw \-\-codec prores input.mov output.mov
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode with a non\-default library and verbose output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-library /data/library \-\-verbose \-\-preset 4k in.mov out.mov
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR badapplestein (1),
.BR badapplestein-build (1)
